  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a fix plan, but I haven't changed any code. Plan mode is on, and the tool for submitting a plan for approval is disabled in this session. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the change.\n\n**Cause:** in `src/click/core.py:392`, a subcommand's context copies its parent's whole `default_map`. The documented format nests each subcommand's defaults under its name, for example `{'runserver': {'port': 5000}}`. The subcommand therefore looks for `port` in the top-level dict and never finds it.\n\n**Planned fix:** change that line to `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. A subcommand then gets its own sub-dict, nested groups work the same way, and a subcommand with no entry gets `None`.\n\n**Tests and docs:**\n- Add tests in `tests/test_defaults.py` for a subcommand, a nested group and a missing key.\n- Add a `CHANGES.md` entry.\n- Run `tests/test_defaults.py`, `tests/test_context.py` and `tests/test_commands.py`.\n- Check that the existing test near `tests/test_defaults.py:434` still passes.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-starry-dongarra.md`.",
